{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CguYifLdaRrFMQ8Vreckg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm approving milestone `optional-worktree-runtime` (roadmap B35). As the notes say, the code hasn't changed since the round-4 approval. The two low findings from round 3 are still in the code unchanged, and I found nothing new.\n\nLike the earlier rounds, I couldn't run `pose validate`, `review-check` or `closeout-check` myself, because the shell is limited to `git status` and `git ls-files`. The validation verdicts below rely on the sealed evidence, and I read the code and reports directly.\n\n**Findings from round 3, both still open (low, follow-up):**\n- **R3-N4, not fixed:** in `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:280` the heavy check run alongside the short queries still throws away its output and route. The T5 verdict at `:378` still says every hosted run matched the standalone output. Two simultaneous heavy checks (`:299-307`) are compared, but this single one is not.\n- **R3-N5, not fixed:** in `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:160-161` the \"busy\" count still goes up before the reply is written. The connection stays counted as in flight until `pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go:369` runs. In that window, `status` can report one command too many in flight and a stop can overstate how many it drained.\n\n**What changed since round 4:** only `.pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md`, which gained the \"Estado (2026-11-10)\" paragraph (lines 15-20) and the member-spec trailers. That paragraph matches the delivery and the ADR's departures. It doesn't affect the exit gate.\n\n**Criteria:**\n- **Exit gate: passed.** The gate is at roadmap line 77. Every hosted request is checked against the caller's identity before any handler runs (`runtime.go:426,449-456`). The OS reports which user owns the connection before anything is read from it (`runtime.go:404-408`). A command is refused, never queued, when its lane is full or its deadline passes (`runtime_host.go:107-119`). The fourth measurement run passes T1–T7: two heavy checks at once take 21266 ms against a limit of 2.5 × 10662 ms, and short queries have a p95 of 10 ms under load. The three departures (no watcher, no retry of hosted reads, no CPU quota or per-command limits) are disclosed in the ADR amendment at line 271.\n- **Integration: passed,** on `integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration` plus the sealed `resident-cache` and `runtime-qos` integration evidence.\n- **Membership: passed.** All three member specs are `status: done` with no unchecked tasks. The resident-cache spec's medium follow-up is marked as covered by the QoS spec.\n- **Regression: passed,** on the sealed `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` and `build:pose-mcp/go/build`.\n- **Residual risk: passed.** The undelivered items have their own draft specs, and only the two low findings above remain open.\n\ndecision: approved\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R3-N4\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:280 still runs runtimeRun(\\\"review-check\\\", spec) and discards output and via; the T5 verdict at :378 is unchanged. Low; it remains the follow-up accepted in round 4 (owner @pose-maintainers). The measured T7 runs (:299-307) do compare heavy output and via.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R3-N5\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:160-161 still increments busy before the handler returns, while runtime.go:369 decrements inflight only after the reply is written; state() at runtime.go:503 and drain() at :472-486 sum both. Low; it remains the follow-up accepted in round 4 (owner @pose-maintainers).\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Re-read the hosted handler and lanes (pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:80-166), the server accept/idle/handle/drain/state path (pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go:330-510), and the measurement harness S5-S6, T3-T5 and T7 (pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:260-384). Checked the four runs in .pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.json (the fourth passes T1-T7), the roadmap including the new Estado paragraph and the B35 exit gate (.pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md:15-20, 63-81), the ADR amendments at lines 239 and 271 including the declared departures, and the status, open tasks and crit follow-ups of the three member specs. Found no new defect. The roadmap edit since round 4 only states the delivered status.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"exit-gate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the B35 gate (roadmap :77-81) against the code and the measurements. Identity is checked at handshake and on every hosted request before the handler (runtime.go:426,449-456); the peer UID is checked before any read (runtime.go:404-408); admission refuses on a full lane or at the deadline (runtime_host.go:107-119); the fourth measurement run passes T1-T7 with RAM, CPU and latency per scenario. The departures (no watcher, so the memo is keyed by commit; no retry of hosted reads; no CPU quota or per-command limits) are disclosed in the ADR amendment at line 271 and in the roadmap. Concluded that the gate has falsifiable evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The runtime, resident-cache and QoS slices compose through one Handler/Busy/Metrics contract in worktreeruntime.Options, and the sealed integration evidence for all three passes (optional-worktree-runtime, resident-cache, runtime-qos).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"membership\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"All three ordered member specs are status: done with no unchecked tasks. The crit:medium follow-up of the resident-cache spec is marked covered by the qos spec. The delivery code is unchanged since the round-4 approval, so the closures remain current.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"regression\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the sealed module validation of pose-mcp: the unit, build and every integration and reachability check pass. Concluded there is no regression.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"residual-risk\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The cross-spec items not delivered (CPU quota/affinity, per-command limits, Windows named pipe, default routing) are in their own draft specs, per the roadmap (:18-20) and the ADR (:301). The only open items are R3-N4 and R3-N5, which are low and remain the follow-ups accepted in round 4.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only. The review profile allows no shell beyond git status and ls-files, so I relied on reading the code.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only. The review profile allows no shell beyond git status and ls-files.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is this review's attestation; POSE runs it after recording.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is this review's attestation; POSE runs it after recording.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only. The review profile allows no shell; I swept the subject by reading it instead.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The strict module validation of pose-mcp is sealed in the bundle (unit, build and all integration and reachability checks pass).\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":40242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":678},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"90c74efc-9589-4006-9d93-36973c36c77d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T16:17:16.473Z","request_id":"req_011CguYif6WQ13ZRSZpzqSkJ"}
